# A rule naming a team that does not exist is SILENTLY DROPPED: the file still
# parses, and reviews for those paths route to nobody. Reading the file cannot
# show this — after every edit here, check
# `gh api /repos/{owner}/{repo}/codeowners/errors`.
#
# EVERY RULE NAMES BOTH SENIOR TEAMS, and a rule's owners are an OR: one
# approval from either team satisfies it. The team listed first is the one whose
# judgment the path normally wants; the second is there so a senior of either
# kind can unblock a PR that spans both. Keep both on every line you add.
#
# Resolution is LAST MATCH WINS. Because every rule carries the same two teams,
# ordering does not currently change who may approve — it would again the moment
# any line names a different set.
#
# THERE IS NO `*` DEFAULT, deliberately. Branch protection requires ONE approval
# from anyone with write access on every PR regardless; a rule here adds the
# requirement that it come from a senior. A path nobody names gets that one
# approval from anyone — it just does not pull a senior into a CSS tweak, an
# icon, or a dotfile. Only claim a path when a senior's judgment is what a
# review of it needs.
#
# THE COUNT DROPPED FROM 2 TO 1 ON 2026-09-16, which raised the stakes on every
# unowned path: what used to get two readers now gets one, and on an unowned
# path that one need not be a senior. So the set of unowned files is no longer
# a matter of taste — it was ENUMERATED against this file rather than asserted.
# 337 of 4573 tracked files match no rule. They are:
#
#   216 .md          docs/ prose and .claude/ lead tooling — deliberate
#    48 .css         styling — deliberate
#    11 .txt         OCR key fixtures under mcp-server/dev/ — deliberate
#     6 .html        slides and two app entry points — deliberate
#   ~50 dotfiles,    .gitignore/.npmrc/.nvmrc/LICENSE/icons/.gitkeep — deliberate
#       icons, misc
#
# Everything else was claimed below. DO NOT re-justify an unowned path from
# memory of this list: re-run the count. The audit is a `git ls-tree` against
# the rules here, and the list rots the moment either side changes.

